      "assertions": "EntryPresentationTests.swift:77–112. A disabled original commit and three invalid batch orderings throw. The invalid batches preserve editor state, document, publication count (0) and exact disk bytes. Shipped wrong event-kind, wrong event-value and over-bound field controls throw and preserve state and bytes. The accepted title, note and entry.commit batch publishes one revision before the disk write. After settle it has two total publications, one entry titled Updated and one entrySaved effect. A separate passive read of workspace.json confirms the stored title, exact Unicode note and single entrySaved record."
    },
    "F15": {
      "selectors": [
        "testActualPostMutationLongNoteProjectionRefusesBeforeDurableWrite",
        "testPrecommitProjectionFailureLeavesSnapshotBytesUntouched"
      ],
      "introducingCommit": "c6562ba80b992016c0c963cf4c67a59f1f605fd0",
      "anchorsVerified": 3,
      "assertions": "EntryPresentationTests.swift:182–209 and PaginationContractTests.swift:120–154. A 100,000-byte UTF-8 EntrySaveIntent validates, then the real in-transaction V3 projection throws limitExceeded(stringBytes), preserving exact disk bytes and leaving zero entries. The companion task projection supplies synthetic over-contract editor state, requires the same error, identical bytes and zero tasks, then verifies a valid retry saves one task, two total outbox records, a matching task record ID and exact decoded disk equality."
    },
    "F16": {
      "selectors": [
        "testCancelledCloseDrainsAdmittedSaveAndReleasesLock"
      ],
      "introducingCommit": "c6562ba80b992016c0c963cf4c67a59f1f605fd0",
      "anchorsVerified": 2,
      "assertions": "PaginationContractTests.swift:156–172. The test sends task.save, cancels the Swift task calling public app close, then reads the exact Unicode task title, responsible party and two total outbox records from disk. Fresh app construction in the same XCTest process reacquires the real nonblocking exclusive flock and reads back the same workspace."
    }
